.md
# Recreation of World of Goo or Bridge Construction Game with WLJS

Here we shall try to model a system of interconnected bonds using the Verlet method. Then, we'll add some visuals to make it feel like a game.

<a href="#tldr-goo">TLDR: actual game</a>

<br/><br/>

## Motion Equations
The system of connected points must obey Newton's laws and kinematic equations as well. To integrate them in real-time, Euler's method, RK (Runge-Kutta), or Verlet methods can be used. We will go for the Verlet method since it will be easier to apply constraints of the bonds in the future:

$$
x_{n+1} = 2 x_{n} - x_{n-1} + \\frac{f_{n}}{m} \\delta t^2
$$

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
